-Phil's main point is that "for this use at least, \magsteps are
-mandatory". I understand from this that it is not a question of plain
-vs. LaTeX -- which is what I suspected from the beginning.

Except that for his use we were talking about scaling 1800 vs
1728 and the like which is not the issue at hand (incidentally
the emTeX drivers are not restricted to magstep values... I
routinely use oddly scaled fonts in bottle label printing) but
rather cmcsc10 scaled 1728 (or cmr17) vs. cmcsc18 (or cmr18).
Which is a horse of a different color and doesn't really apply as
near as I can tell to Phil's application.

But it's still not plain vs. LaTeX anyway.

-dh


